/-!
# Actual phase-collapse spaces and maps for the cusp central fibre

The central toric fibre is the genuine proper quotient of the compact
fibre torus times its positive part. Its exact phase fibres are a
two-torus, a circle, or a point on the three central strata; the collapsed
subgroups are respectively trivial, the primitive vertex-difference
circle, and the whole compact fibre torus.

Adding the explicit positive lattice translation and frozen compact
phase gives a quotient model homeomorphic to the literal central fibre
of the original cusp quotient. This establishes the geometric phase
identifications used in Lemma 7.10 without assuming a model or its
topology. A global honeycomb parameterization and the prescribed
fixed-nonzero-fibre specialization map remain separate constructions.
-/
